Theorem CH-1: Burden-registry-lattice composition soundness

  Preconditions:
    - F is an ArcFunction in scope of docs/ori_lang/proposals/approved/aims-burden-tracking-proposal.md
      burden-prototype minimal-lattice-consumer
    - BR is the burden-registry typed pre-pass output for F
      (per-variable burden annotations consumed by the consumer
       per the burden-prototype design)
    - L is the converged AimsStateMap for F per IA-7
    - consume_stack(F, BR, L) is the burden-elimination consumer:
      walks F's instruction stream; for each variable v with burden
      entries in BR, validates the elimination decision (DP-2 dec
      unnecessary OR DP-3 inc elidable) against L[v]'s converged
      lattice state
    - Lean 4 cross-validation MANDATORY per the dual-prover Lean formalization
      critical-proof set (the Lean 4 cross-validation strategy)

  Soundness property:
    Forall v in vars(F).
      consume_stack(F, BR, L)[v] is consistent with L[v] under
      DP-2 (is_rc_dec_unnecessary) and DP-3 (is_rc_inc_elidable);
      i.e. no double-counting (burden writes do not race-invalidate
      elimination decisions);
      per-class coexistence well-formedness holds (lattice classes +
      burden classes do not overlap in their elimination claims).

  Proof obligation:
    Structural induction over F's instruction stream:
      Base case: F's first instruction.
        BR pre-pass already populated (typed input per Annex E §AIMS
        sec-Non-Negotiable-Invariants invariant 5(c) "typed pre-pass
        input that lands on AimsStateMap");
        L's block_entry_states for F.entry seeded by IA backward
        walk;
        consume_stack invariant: no elimination decisions emitted
        before any instruction processed (vacuously true).
      Inductive step over instruction i_k:
        Assume consume_stack invariant holds at position k-1.
        For instruction i_k defining/using v:
          (a) BR pre-pass entry for v (if any) read from typed
              side-table (NOT a lattice dimension per Annex E §AIMS
              invariant 5);
          (b) L[v] at position k consulted for canonical state;
          (c) DP-2 evaluated on L[v]: if is_rc_dec_unnecessary
              (cardinality = Absent OR consumption = Dead), the
              burden-registry SHALL agree (no burden write for
              this v at this point);
          (d) DP-3 evaluated on L[v]: if is_rc_inc_elidable
              (cardinality = 1 AND (consumption = L OR consumption = A)),
              the burden-registry SHALL agree;
          (e) on disagreement, consume_stack returns an
              inconsistency diagnostic (this CH-1 theorem proves
              no inconsistency arises under well-formed BR + L).

    Interprocedural summary (burden-registry-as-typed-pre-pass +
    DP-2/DP-3 elimination contract):
      BR is computed by a pass that depends on AimsStateMap L
      (per the burden-prototype design); the pass is acyclic w.r.t. L
      (BR pre-pass reads L, not vice versa);
      no fixpoint cycle between BR and L;
      contract: BR's writes are sound w.r.t. L's converged state.

    Case analysis on per-class coexistence well-formedness
    (lattice class C_L vs burden class C_B):
      Case C_L disjoint from C_B (no variable v in both):
        Trivially well-formed; no overlap; no race.
      Case v in both C_L and C_B:
        C_L (lattice class) records v's canonical lattice state;
        C_B (burden class) records v's burden annotation;
        Well-formedness: BR's annotation for v must be consistent
        with L[v]'s elimination decision per DP-2 + DP-3;
        Inconsistency = CH-1 violation = burden-prototype design bug.

    Lattice composition (sec-02 lattice transfer composition):
      Per sec-02, lattice transfer functions compose per L-6
      monotonicity; consume_stack walks the instruction stream
      with both L (lattice) and BR (burden) inputs, applying
      DP-2 / DP-3 at each variable's use point;
      composition is sound because L and BR are independent typed
      inputs to consume_stack (no shared mutable state).

    Engines dispatched:
      structural_induction (instruction-stream walk + per-instruction
                            invariant maintenance for consume_stack)
      interprocedural_summary (BR-as-typed-pre-pass + DP-2/DP-3
                               elimination contract; SCC topological
                               order if F's CH burden depends on
                               callees' contracts)
      case_analysis (per-class coexistence well-formedness branches
                     + DP-2/DP-3 disagreement vs agreement)
      lattice (sec-02 lattice transfer composition; L's
               per-dimension canonicalization preserved by
               consume_stack's read-only access)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: sec-11 section_11 engine discharges CH-shape; structural_induction + interprocedural_summary + case_analysis + lattice (PRIMARY by CH-N) + refinement + rc_counting + monotonicity + fixpoint (SECONDARY gracious-accept) constructively verify the coexistence-handshake composition per the §11 coexistence section Per-CH Proof-Status Tracking table
